                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I guess the sad responsibility rests on me to write what seems to be the first full Steam review for Jammerball.   Jammerball is a fictional sports game based loosely on dodgeball.  You have two players per side, and you have two balls.  The objective is to hit the other players with your balls and their balls until they are exhausted from all the balls.   The developers added 8 teams (you can choose your team from those but you can't customize it).   The team you choose has little bearing on the kinds of balls you have (see what I did there? Bearings? Balls? Ball bearings!), but each team does have a specific skin for the arena so the devs put a little effort in there.\n\nOn to the unfortunate reasons I cannot ultimately recommend this game.   The game assets are really low quality.  The characters all start out t-posed, and the animations aren't much better.  Controls are clunky and awkward.  Gameplay look and feel is very low quality.   The game does feature a reasonably decent rendering of each teams balls.",
